  "baseline": "axum with Tokio's default multi-threaded runtime: TechEmpower Round 22 entry (axum 0.6.16, hyper 0.14) and HttpArena 2026 standard-mode entry (axum 0.8)",
  "verdict": "downgrade",
  "verdict_reason": "actix-web is faster than default-config axum in both benchmarks, 1.13x to 2.57x on trivial handlers. With a database in the path (TechEmpower fortunes, both on deadpool-postgres) the lead is 15%, and actix failed to start in Round 23, so there is no comparison against the thread-per-core axum that caught up with ntex and xitca-web.",
  "evidence_tier": "A",
  "tier_reason": "Two public benchmarks with published implementation code and stated hardware: TechEmpower Round 22 and HttpArena.",
  "claimed_speedup": "TechEmpower Round 22 peak total requests per 15 s, actix vs axum: plaintext 64827336 vs 57504288, JSON 17109800 vs 11657647, fortunes (actix-web-pg-deadpool vs axum-pg-pool) 1458364 vs 1269748 (1.13x, 1.47x, 1.15x) (derived from page data). HttpArena, req/s actix vs axum: baseline-4096 2775120 vs 1080638, json-tls-4096 1157219 vs 967831, json-comp-4096 541211 vs 268142, pipelined-4096 16338425 vs 6474608 (2.57x, 1.20x, 2.02x, 2.52x) (derived from page data)",
  "workload": "TechEmpower plaintext (pipelined), JSON and fortunes (Postgres + HTML template), peak req/s over 15-second runs. HttpArena: mixed GET/POST with query parsing, JSON over TLS, JSON with gzip/brotli, and 16x pipelined requests, all at 4,096 connections.",
  "metric": "throughput",
  "hardware": "TechEmpower Round 22 (Citrine): three machines with 28 HT cores Intel Xeon Gold 5120 @ 2.20GHz, 32 GB, switched 10-gigabit Ethernet. HttpArena: one AMD Threadripper PRO 3995WX workstation (64 cores).",
  "os": "Linux, in Docker",
  "toolchain": "Round 22: actix-web 4.3.1, RUSTFLAGS=\"-C target-cpu=native\", lto, codegen-units 1; axum 0.6.16 on rust:1.67, target-cpu=native. HttpArena: actix-web 4 from git and axum 0.8 on rust:1.94, opt-level 3, codegen-units 1, lto thin.",
  "benchmark_date": "2026-09",
  "benchmark_url": "https://www.http-arena.com/",
  "repo_url": "https://github.com/actix/actix-web",
  "docs_url": "https://docs.rs/actix-web",
